1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:03,640
It's 1:30 in the morning, you're in bed,

2
00:00:03,680 --> 00:00:09,050
and the classic late-night thumb
workout begins on your phone.

3
00:00:09,240 --> 00:00:15,120
You open a first video: someone is
holding an injector pen in their

4
00:00:15,160 --> 00:00:16,710
hand and says:

5
00:00:16,960 --> 00:00:21,420
“One shot, zero appetite,
I melted in half.”

6
00:00:21,460 --> 00:00:23,920
One little flick of the thumb upward,

7
00:00:23,960 --> 00:00:28,120
and bam, second video: “I used this pen.

8
00:00:28,160 --> 00:00:30,630
Surprise, I got pregnant.”

9
00:00:31,160 --> 00:00:34,010
Look closely: between these two videos,

10
00:00:34,160 --> 00:00:36,890
there is only one thumb movement.

11
00:00:37,993 --> 00:00:39,247
0.2 seconds.

12
00:00:39,960 --> 00:00:43,660
Watching that, you immediately think:

13
00:00:43,700 --> 00:00:47,800
“Well, that's settled: take
the shot, have the baby.”

14
00:00:47,840 --> 00:00:54,140
But scientifically, establishing
that link takes a tiny

15
00:00:54,180 --> 00:00:57,950
bit more work than swiping a screen.

16
00:00:58,200 --> 00:01:05,000
Medications in the GLP-1
family can indeed contribute

17
00:01:05,040 --> 00:01:09,960
indirectly to pregnancy
chances in some women.

18
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:16,160
But they are absolutely not
direct infertility treatments.

19
00:01:16,300 --> 00:01:19,970
And they are not used during pregnancy.

20
00:01:20,160 --> 00:01:23,133
I'm Dr. Senai Aksoy.

21
00:01:23,580 --> 00:01:29,720
Today, let's look together at the real
link between these famous injections

22
00:01:29,760 --> 00:01:36,300
and fertility, and above all
what to watch out for when

23
00:01:36,340 --> 00:01:38,360
planning a baby.

24
00:01:38,400 --> 00:01:40,250
Let's start from the beginning.

25
00:01:40,700 --> 00:01:43,087
What is GLP-1?

26
00:01:43,595 --> 00:01:49,280
The name sounds a bit like the
latest model of a hybrid car,

27
00:01:49,320 --> 00:01:55,440
but in reality, it's a natural
hormone our body produces

28
00:01:55,480 --> 00:01:57,500
after meals.

29
00:01:57,540 --> 00:02:03,740
It plays a key role in fullness
and blood sugar regulation,

30
00:02:03,780 --> 00:02:08,110
by sending a very simple
message to the brain:

31
00:02:08,153 --> 00:02:10,700
“All good, boss, we're full.

32
00:02:10,740 --> 00:02:15,410
Put the fork down gently,
blood sugar is under control.”

33
00:02:15,990 --> 00:02:20,170
Medications like semaglutide and

34
00:02:20,850 --> 00:02:25,850
liraglutide act as the official
stunt doubles of this hormone.

35
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:27,830
They mimic its action.

36
00:02:28,100 --> 00:02:32,060
Tirzepatide, for its
part, shows up as a team.

37
00:02:32,100 --> 00:02:40,030
In addition to GLP-1, it draws on the
effect of another hormone called GIP.

38
00:02:40,830 --> 00:02:46,220
In eligible people, it can
help with weight management and

39
00:02:46,260 --> 00:02:48,010
blood sugar control.

40
00:02:48,220 --> 00:02:49,000
Very good.

41
00:02:49,040 --> 00:02:53,560
But how do we get from
there to a pregnancy?

42
00:02:53,600 --> 00:02:58,590
Much of it plays out in
polycystic ovary syndrome,

43
00:02:58,660 --> 00:03:00,240
the famous PCOS.

44
00:03:00,280 --> 00:03:04,130
In some women with PCOS,

45
00:03:04,200 --> 00:03:10,560
insulin resistance and
ovulation problems walk

46
00:03:10,600 --> 00:03:11,800
hand in hand.

47
00:03:11,840 --> 00:03:17,640
Insulin resistance is
when insulin knocks on the

48
00:03:17,680 --> 00:03:21,810
cell's door and nobody
answers from inside.

49
00:03:21,880 --> 00:03:26,190
The body doesn't respond
enough to insulin.

50
00:03:26,280 --> 00:03:31,050
When metabolic health and
weight management improve,

51
00:03:31,200 --> 00:03:33,990
that inner chaos settles down.

52
00:03:34,120 --> 00:03:39,480
In some women, periods
become more regular and the

53
00:03:39,520 --> 00:03:44,120
ovaries say, “Hey, it's calm
again in here, how about we

54
00:03:44,160 --> 00:03:45,840
start ovulating?”

55
00:03:45,880 --> 00:03:48,930
The contribution to pregnancy chances,

56
00:03:48,980 --> 00:03:52,110
at least in part, may come from there.

57
00:03:52,300 --> 00:03:55,700
But beware of the classic shortcut:

58
00:03:55,740 --> 00:04:01,130
not all women with PCOS are overweight,

59
00:04:01,180 --> 00:04:06,290
and not all overweight women
have an ovulation problem.

60
00:04:06,760 --> 00:04:11,260
So we can't set up the automatic equation

61
00:04:11,300 --> 00:04:16,330
“I have PCOS, so I need this injection.”

62
00:04:16,660 --> 00:04:20,540
So, are the studies encouraging?

63
00:04:20,580 --> 00:04:21,770
Some are, yes.

64
00:04:21,980 --> 00:04:24,910
In women with PCOS,

65
00:04:25,040 --> 00:04:30,870
some research shows
improved cycle regularity

66
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:33,950
and spontaneous pregnancy rates.

67
00:04:34,060 --> 00:04:39,540
But some of these studies involve
small numbers of patients,

68
00:04:39,580 --> 00:04:44,390
with different medications
and add-on treatments.

69
00:04:44,620 --> 00:04:50,080
And the fact that one single person
on social media gets pregnant

70
00:04:50,120 --> 00:04:54,960
after taking this drug does
not directly prove that egg

71
00:04:55,000 --> 00:04:56,950
quality has improved.

72
00:04:57,180 --> 00:04:59,330
That is not scientific proof.

73
00:04:59,560 --> 00:05:01,610
That's coffee-machine chat.

74
00:05:02,270 --> 00:05:07,380
Besides, the results don't all
point in the same direction.

75
00:05:07,420 --> 00:05:11,410
In a registry study published in 2026,

76
00:05:11,540 --> 00:05:17,680
of women with infertility
associated with overweight

77
00:05:17,720 --> 00:05:23,760
or obesity, semaglutide use was associated

78
00:05:23,800 --> 00:05:29,490
with lower pregnancy and live birth rates.

79
00:05:29,820 --> 00:05:35,280
No hasty conclusions: this
is an observational study.

80
00:05:35,320 --> 00:05:40,710
So we cannot claim that the
drug is the direct cause.

81
00:05:40,840 --> 00:05:46,780
Factors such as treatment timing
and voluntarily postponing

82
00:05:46,820 --> 00:05:52,210
pregnancy may well have
influenced these results.

83
00:05:52,400 --> 00:05:56,740
Don't mix them up: getting
regular cycles back,

84
00:05:56,780 --> 00:06:02,980
ovulating, having a positive
pregnancy test and achieving a live

85
00:06:03,020 --> 00:06:06,720
birth are quite distinct outcomes.

86
00:06:06,760 --> 00:06:11,580
We cannot extrapolate these
observations to all women,

87
00:06:11,620 --> 00:06:17,910
to all GLP-1 medications, or
to in vitro fertilization.

88
00:06:18,100 --> 00:06:24,140
We do not have strong and
sufficient evidence showing that

89
00:06:24,180 --> 00:06:30,830
GLP-1 agonists increase the
chances of a live birth in IVF.

90
00:06:30,900 --> 00:06:37,100
The 2023 international PCOS
guidelines actually make

91
00:06:37,140 --> 00:06:39,550
this distinction clearly.

92
00:06:39,920 --> 00:06:44,960
These medications may be
considered for weight management in

93
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:51,140
eligible people, but their use to improve

94
00:06:51,180 --> 00:06:57,710
fertility outcomes in PCOS remains
limited to research settings.

95
00:06:58,040 --> 00:07:04,020
The clinical decision must rest on
an appropriate medical indication

96
00:07:04,060 --> 00:07:07,580
such as weight management or diabetes.

97
00:07:07,620 --> 00:07:14,073
If not getting pregnant with
PCOS is due solely to a lack

98
00:07:14,113 --> 00:07:19,610
of ovulation, and no other cause
of infertility is identified,

99
00:07:19,740 --> 00:07:24,540
the first-line ovulation
induction treatment recommended

100
00:07:24,580 --> 00:07:29,060
by medical guidelines is letrozole.

101
00:07:29,240 --> 00:07:31,890
Now here is a crucial point.

102
00:07:32,420 --> 00:07:35,660
Some patients calmly tell themselves:

103
00:07:35,700 --> 00:07:38,630
“Doctor, I get my period
every three months,

104
00:07:38,840 --> 00:07:41,740
I'm not at risk of getting pregnant.”

105
00:07:41,780 --> 00:07:43,820
Don't think that at all.

106
00:07:43,860 --> 00:07:48,530
The body ovulates first;
the period comes afterwards.

107
00:07:48,600 --> 00:07:54,490
When ovulation restarts, your ovaries
don't send you a text to warn you.

108
00:07:54,680 --> 00:07:59,370
A pregnancy can happen at a
completely unexpected moment.

109
00:07:59,580 --> 00:08:05,280
Yet we do not have sufficient
human data to state

110
00:08:05,320 --> 00:08:08,470
that these medications
are safe during pregnancy.

111
00:08:08,760 --> 00:08:14,060
Effective contraception is therefore
essential during treatment and

112
00:08:14,100 --> 00:08:17,910
during the stopping period
specific to each medication.

113
00:08:18,040 --> 00:08:19,420
What is the timeline?

114
00:08:19,460 --> 00:08:24,900
For semaglutide, it is recommended
to stop it at least two months

115
00:08:24,940 --> 00:08:27,430
before a planned pregnancy.

116
00:08:27,480 --> 00:08:32,590
For tirzepatide, this interval
is at least one month.

117
00:08:32,680 --> 00:08:38,760
The medication used, the date of the
last dose and the exact timing of

118
00:08:38,800 --> 00:08:44,640
when to start trying must be
clarified with the prescribing doctor.

119
00:08:44,680 --> 00:08:50,200
And if you have diabetes,
blood sugar treatment suited to

120
00:08:50,240 --> 00:08:53,660
pregnancy absolutely must be planned.

121
00:08:53,700 --> 00:08:57,120
For those using tirzepatide,

122
00:08:57,460 --> 00:09:03,180
there is a very important
detail, especially in people with

123
00:09:03,220 --> 00:09:05,950
overweight and obesity.

124
00:09:06,730 --> 00:09:11,260
The effectiveness of the birth
control pill may decrease.

125
00:09:11,300 --> 00:09:15,950
Because these medications
change how the stomach empties,

126
00:09:16,510 --> 00:09:19,030
absorption of the pill can drop.

127
00:09:19,120 --> 00:09:23,240
So using an additional
method is recommended,

128
00:09:23,280 --> 00:09:27,470
such as a condom on top of the pill,

129
00:09:27,540 --> 00:09:33,660
for the four weeks after
starting treatment and for the

130
00:09:33,700 --> 00:09:38,560
four weeks after each dose
increase, or switching to

131
00:09:38,600 --> 00:09:40,740
a non-oral contraceptive.

132
00:09:40,780 --> 00:09:46,320
Note: this warning is not the same for all

133
00:09:46,360 --> 00:09:48,330
GLP-1 medications.

134
00:09:49,340 --> 00:09:54,670
And what if the pregnancy test
turns positive during treatment?

135
00:09:55,180 --> 00:09:59,850
Contact the prescribing doctor
and your OB-GYN immediately.

136
00:10:00,120 --> 00:10:03,250
This medication is not
continued during pregnancy.

137
00:10:03,300 --> 00:10:08,620
But having been exposed to the
drug doesn't mean the baby has

138
00:10:08,660 --> 00:10:10,740
necessarily been harmed.

139
00:10:10,780 --> 00:10:16,970
Available human data are
reassuring in some respects,

140
00:10:17,040 --> 00:10:23,470
but not robust enough to
guarantee pregnancy safety.

141
00:10:24,267 --> 00:10:26,780
The medication used is then assessed,

142
00:10:26,820 --> 00:10:31,230
along with the dose and the stage
of pregnancy when it was taken.

143
00:10:31,670 --> 00:10:36,540
If you have diabetes, an alternative
treatment is started without delay.

144
00:10:36,580 --> 00:10:41,160
Before in vitro fertilization, age,

145
00:10:41,300 --> 00:10:47,440
ovarian reserve, the cause of
infertility and the impact of

146
00:10:47,480 --> 00:10:53,390
the waiting time on fertility
must be assessed together.

147
00:10:53,840 --> 00:10:57,360
Telling everyone “lose weight first,

148
00:10:57,400 --> 00:11:00,820
we'll see about treatment
later” isn't right.

149
00:11:00,860 --> 00:11:06,580
For some people, metabolic
preparation makes sense.

150
00:11:06,620 --> 00:11:11,450
For others, delaying care for
a long time isn't appropriate.

151
00:11:11,520 --> 00:11:16,500
Your weight is not a grade on a
report card that decides whether you

152
00:11:16,540 --> 00:11:19,140
deserve treatment or not.

153
00:11:19,180 --> 00:11:22,960
And if an egg retrieval is planned,

154
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:29,830
be sure to tell the IVF team and the

155
00:11:29,980 --> 00:11:30,980
anesthesiologist about your treatment.

156
00:11:31,820 --> 00:11:35,220
Never tell yourself: “It's
just my weight-loss pen,

157
00:11:35,260 --> 00:11:37,900
of course, no need to mention it.”

158
00:11:37,940 --> 00:11:41,370
These medications slow
down stomach emptying.

159
00:11:41,540 --> 00:11:44,690
Even if you've fasted for eight hours,

160
00:11:45,160 --> 00:11:51,050
the stomach may not be empty,
which is crucial during sedation or

161
00:11:51,090 --> 00:11:52,120
anesthesia.

162
00:11:52,160 --> 00:11:56,990
The stopping plan for pregnancy
and pre-anesthesia protocols

163
00:11:57,180 --> 00:11:59,370
are two different things.

164
00:12:00,250 --> 00:12:04,670
Let your team draw up
your personalized plan.

165
00:12:04,950 --> 00:12:07,150
And then, there are the men.

166
00:12:07,200 --> 00:12:13,500
Gentlemen, don't watch this video
from the corner of the couch saying:

167
00:12:13,540 --> 00:12:16,830
“See, honey, the doctor
is talking to you.”

168
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:19,420
In men with obesity,

169
00:12:19,460 --> 00:12:24,820
lifestyle changes such
as diet and physical

170
00:12:24,860 --> 00:12:30,450
activity can improve
certain sperm parameters.

171
00:12:30,540 --> 00:12:35,150
There is also research
on GLP-1 medications,

172
00:12:35,440 --> 00:12:38,010
but the evidence remains limited.

173
00:12:38,640 --> 00:12:42,620
Today, we cannot present
these medications as a

174
00:12:42,660 --> 00:12:45,580
proven treatment for male infertility.

175
00:12:45,620 --> 00:12:49,660
Side effects, such as nausea,

176
00:12:49,700 --> 00:12:52,400
vomiting and digestive problems,

177
00:12:52,440 --> 00:12:54,540
may also occur.

178
00:12:54,580 --> 00:12:57,620
And weight regain is possible,

179
00:12:57,660 --> 00:13:01,165
unfortunately, after
stopping the medication.

180
00:13:01,660 --> 00:13:04,590
That's why diet, physical activity,

181
00:13:04,800 --> 00:13:10,120
metabolic follow-up and the
transition to pregnancy must be

182
00:13:10,160 --> 00:13:12,080
planned together.

183
00:13:12,120 --> 00:13:18,470
In short, clarify these three
points with your doctor.

184
00:13:19,060 --> 00:13:23,270
1. Why do I medically
need this medication?

185
00:13:23,360 --> 00:13:27,840
2. When should I stop it
before trying to conceive,

186
00:13:27,880 --> 00:13:32,250
and how do I ensure
contraception during that time?

187
00:13:32,480 --> 00:13:38,660
3. How does this affect the
timeline of my fertility treatment?

188
00:13:38,700 --> 00:13:44,700
So, lastly, this content
is provided for information

189
00:13:44,740 --> 00:13:50,530
and does not replace an
individual medical evaluation.

190
00:13:51,260 --> 00:13:52,260
Ciao!
